==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|hungur|lang=is}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsvauŋkʏr/|lang=is}}
* {{rhymes|auŋkʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|is|non|svangr||slender, slim, thin}}, from {{m|non|svangi||the groins}}, also spelled {{m|non|svangr}}.

Cognates with the Faroese {{m|fo|svangur||hungry}},<ref name="blondal">{{R:Íslensk orðsifjabók 1989}}</ref> German {{m|de|schlank}}, Nynorsk {{m|nn|svang}},<ref name="blondal" /> dialectal Swedish {{m|sv|svånger}},<ref name="blondal" /> Middle Swedish {{m|sv|svanger||slender, emaciated, very thin}}.<ref name="blondal" />

It went from meaning "slender" ({{m|is|innsveigður}}, {{m|is|sveigður}}, {{m|is|kviðdreginn}}) to meaning "hungry" ({{m|is|magatómur}}, {{m|is|soltinn}}).<ref name="blondal" />

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|svengri|comp2=svangari|svengstur|sup2=svangastur}}

# [[hungry]], [[peckish]]
#: ''Ertu '''svöng'''?''
#:: Are you '''hungry'''?
#: ''Ég er mjög '''svangur'''.''
#:: I'm really '''hungry'''.
# {{lb|is|obsolete}} [[thin]], [[slender]], [[slim]]

